ac{{y}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1$" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534903 true] [17592186318622 1111 #uuid "7b0f6e1b-1d8d-5ba1-b9b5-d4274a290cfa" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318623 1034 "A family of ellipsoids: $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}+{z}^{2}=1$" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534903 true] [17592186318623 1111 #uuid "6e2870f3-bd85-5dec-9116-464f03afc8bf" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1017 #edb/ref 17592186318625 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1089 "q-71596" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1100 "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2}$ that passes through the point $P(4,2,1).$" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1113 #uuid "0c7e17bc-81d9-5d3a-a5a3-3325aa70370c" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318624 1145 "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,2,1) & ={4}^{2}+3(2-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=18.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(4,2,1)$ is the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18}=1.$" 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318626 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318627 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318628 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318629 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318630 13194139534903 true] [17592186318625 1040 #edb/ref 175